**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests`
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests`, `BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests`

**How to implement.** The tabulated n,k table becomes an axis case of the core, and the import builds it (001 §B; .spec-md §3.1). The kernel MOVES from Storage into the core in this step, so one implementation exists. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`, before `EpsAxisDispersion` (`:365`): (a) `TabulatedInterpolation`, a one-case union `LinearInWaveLengthClamped` (linear in λ, clamped to the end samples), with `member value : int` = 1 and `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : TabulatedInterpolation option` answering `None` for any other tag. (b) `TabulatedTableError` with `EmptyTableErr`, `SampleCountMismatchErr` and `UnsortedSamplesErr`, each `of reason : string` naming the counts or the first offending index. (c) `TabulatedNkTable`, a record marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier("...")>]` with `wavelengths : float<meter> array` (ascending), `n : float array`, `k : float array` and `interpolation : TabulatedInterpolation`. `static member tryCreate (wavelengths : float<meter> array) (n : float array) (k : float array) : Result<TabulatedNkTable, TabulatedTableError>` refuses an empty table, columns of unequal length and a wavelength column that decreases anywhere, sets `interpolation = LinearInWaveLengthClamped`, and does not sort. `member sampleRange : WaveLengthInterval` answers the first to the last sample, each as `WaveLength.nm`. `member complexIndex (w : WaveLength) : ComplexRefractionIndex` is the arithmetic of `buildTabulatedClosure` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:160-179`) moved verbatim, answering the index instead of its `Eps`: a one-sample table answers that sample; at or below the first sample, the first; at or above the last, the last; otherwise the same forward scan for the bracketing pair, with t = (λ − a)/(b − a) and t = 0 when the pair shares one wavelength. (d) `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `TabulatedNK of TabulatedNkTable`, and `complexIndex` (`:371-378`) calls the table. While the custom equality stays (until step 9), `Equals` (`:380-388`) compares two `TabulatedNK` values structurally and `GetHashCode` (`:390-394`) hashes the table structurally. The doc comment at `:346-356` names the new case. (2) Every match on `EpsAxisDispersion` follows the new case: `DispersionModel.parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:427-435`) answers `[]` for it, because a table has no editable term scalars; `EpsAxisDispersion.facetKey` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:91-95`) answers `DiscreteKey "Tabulated n/k"`; and `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864-871`) treats it as the evaluated case is treated, as data that is not editable term data. Their doc comments name the new case. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs`: `entryFromTabulated` (`:183-194`) sorts its rows by wavelength with the `Array.sortBy` `buildTabulatedClosure` used (`:159`), builds the table through `TabulatedNkTable.tryCreate`, and answers `Result<MaterialEntry, ImportError>`; a `TabulatedTableError` maps to `NoDataErr` carrying its reason. The entry's `complexity` is `Some` with one isotropic dispersive segment over `table.sampleRange` whose axis is `TabulatedNK table`, `magnetic = None` and `active = None`, and `properties = complexity.toProperties`, as `entryOfAxis` (`:455-469`) does for formula imports. The two call sites (`:502`, `:544`) drop their `Ok` wrapper. `buildTabulatedClosure` is deleted. The closure wording of the module doc (`:18-26`) and of `entryFromTabulated` (`:190-192`) is rewritten, and `NkTableRow`'s carrier reason (`:84`) no longer names a closure. Formula imports are untouched. A tabulated import now has a defined band, its sample range, so the out-of-band diagnostic flags a request outside it (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:166-177`). This is intended: outside its range the table clamps. (4) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains five: `A tabulated axis returns each sample at its own wavelength and interpolates linearly between neighbours`, `A tabulated axis clamps to its first sample below the table and to its last sample above it`, `A single-sample tabulated axis is constant at every wavelength`, `TabulatedNkTable tryCreate refuses an empty table, unequal columns and a decreasing wavelength column` and `The tabulated interpolation rule round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag`. They use a hand-written table (for example 400, 500 and 700 nm, n 1.50, 1.60 and 1.90, k 0.00, 0.10 and 0.30), compute each expected value in the fact, and compare through `BerremanTests.MatrixComparison`'s helpers. The interpolating fact also builds the engine `Eps` through `EpsWithDispValue.toEpsWithDisp` and compares it with `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of the interpolated index. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs` gains `a tabulated axis lands on the tabulated n,k facet key`. `MaterialImportTests` gains `the imported table holds the samples sorted by wavelength in metres under the linear clamped rule`, which matches `TabulatedNK table` on the `Si.yml` import and checks its three columns against the fixture rows. No number moves: step 1's facts are the proof.

**Acceptance.** After the table becomes axis data, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the two MaterialImportTests facts step 1 left red, `tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours`, the two new facts, and every other MaterialImportTests, LibraryFacetsTests and ExportImportTests fact; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass with the five new tabulated facts; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.
